<Weblab2>
  <config><![CDATA[{
  "published": true,
  "game_id": 74,
  "created_at": "2025-11-25T18:08:08.000Z",
  "level_num": "custom",
  "user_id": 18603,
  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "# Build a Moderator Bot\r\n\r\nUse the CHAT Framework to create a simple filter and sorting moderation algorithm for a popular discussion board site.\r\n\r\n### 1. Clarify\r\n* Inspect the data in the code, and decompose ways that you might filter and sort this data.\r\n* Decide what your algorithm values most.\r\n\r\n### 2. Hone / Apply (Build the Filter)\r\n* Determine how you want to filter this data \r\n* Work with AI Tutor to implement a filtering function.\r\n\r\n### 3. Hone / Apply (Build the Sorter)\r\n* Sort the data that remains by an algorithm of your design.\r\n* Work with AI Tutor to implement a sorting function.\r\n\r\n### 4. Hone / Apply (Create the Pipeline)\r\n* Connect the pipeline at the bottom: sort > filter > render\r\n* Ask AI Tutor to generate test cases in order to check for proper implementation and inclusiveness.\r\n\r\n### 5. Transfer\r\n* Create a generalizable system prompt that will create a basic *filter > sort > render* pipeline. Save it into your backpack.\r\n",
    "submittable": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
    "widget_view": "false",
    "initial_view_mode": "split",
    "disable_edit_run_for_submission": "false",
    "ai_tutor_mode": "engineer",
    "predict_settings": {
      "isPredictLevel": false,
      "solution": "",
      "questionType": "freeResponse",
      "allowMultipleAttempts": false,
      "placeholderText": "",
